content.text:
Here is the complete trace. Headline finding first, because it overturns the framing in the prompt: **the mega menu is not an SFCC category tree with Contentful merged in — it is 100% Contentful, and the SFCC category-tree fetch that still exists in `_app/index.tsx` is fetched but explicitly unused by both nav components.** Details and line numbers below.

## 0. Corrected inventory — what the named starting points actually are

| Named in prompt | Reality |
|---|---|
| `overrides/app/hooks/use-navigation.ts` | **Does not exist.** No file matches `*navigation*` anywhere under `overrides/app/`. The only `useNavigation` in play is the unmodified vendor hook `@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/hooks/use-navigation`, imported directly in `overrides/app/components/header/index.tsx:9`. It returns a `navigate()` function for client-side routing (used once, at `header/index.tsx:223`, for the post-logout redirect) — it has nothing to do with menu/category data. |
| `overrides/app/hooks/use-multi-site.ts` | **Does not exist** as an override either. It's the unmodified vendor hook `@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/hooks/use-multi-site`, imported directly by `useHeaderNav.ts:2`, `_app/index.tsx:69`, and `ui-kits/atoms/zimmNavItem/index.tsx:4`. It supplies `{ site, locale, buildUrl }` — used by the real nav hook only to pick which Contentful region/locale to query. |
| `overrides/app/types/commerce.ts`, `components.ts`, `hooks.ts` | **None exist.** `overrides/app/types/` contains exactly two files: `contentful.ts` (has the real nav-item shape) and `vendor.d.ts` (unrelated ambient `react-router-dom` `NavLink` typing, confirmed via grep — no nav/menu content). |
| `overrides/app/theme/components/listMenu.ts`, `header.ts` | **Neither file exists.** `overrides/app/theme/components/` contains `headerShared.ts`, `navConstants.ts`, `footerShared.ts`, `zimmDrawerShared.ts`, `index.ts`, `recipeGuards.test.ts` — no `listMenu.ts`/`header.ts`. The actual Chakra recipes are co-located with their components instead (see §6) and aggregated in `theme/components/index.ts`. |
| `overrides/app/components/header/`, `list-menu/`, `drawer-menu/` | All exist and are exactly what the docs say (Tier 2, mega-menu/nav shell). Confirmed populated, not stubs. |

## 1. Top-down data flow (container → presentational, per file)

**`overrides/app/components/_app/index.tsx`** (root layout container; not in your list but is the actual top of the tree)
- Line 14: `import { useAccessToken, useCategory, useShopperBasketsMutation, useUsid } from '@salesforce/commerce-sdk-react';`
- Lines 161–164:
  ```ts
  const { data: categoriesTree } = useCategory({
    parameters: { id: CAT_MENU_DEFAULT_ROOT_CATEGORY, levels: CAT_MENU_DEFAULT_NAV_SSR_DEPTH },
  });
  const categories = flatten((categoriesTree || {}) as CategoryNode, 'categories');
  ```
  (`CAT_MENU_DEFAULT_ROOT_CATEGORY = 'root'`, `CAT_MENU_DEFAULT_NAV_SSR_DEPTH = 1`, from `node_modules/@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/constants.js:45-46`.) **This is the SFCC category-tree call the prompt asked about — it exists, but it's in `_app/index.tsx`, not in any hook, and not in a file named `use-navigation.ts`.**
- Lines 428–437: renders `<DrawerMenu root={categories?.[CAT_MENU_DEFAULT_ROOT_CATEGORY]} itemsKey="categories" itemsCountKey="onlineSubCategoriesCount" itemComponent={DrawerMenuItemWithData}>` inside `<Header>`.
- Lines 440–445: renders `<ListMenu root={categories?.[CAT_MENU_DEFAULT_ROOT_CATEGORY]} itemsKey="categories" itemsCountKey="onlineSubCategoriesCount" contentComponent={ListMenuContentWithData}>`, also inside `<Header>` as its `children`.
- This is exactly the base-template contract (`_app.jsx` passes the category tree as `root`/`itemsKey`/`itemsCountKey` down to `ListMenu`/`DrawerMenu`). **Both the Zimmermann-overridden `ListMenu` and `DrawerMenu` now ignore every one of those props** (see below) — so `categoriesTree`/`categories` and the two `withCommerceSdkReact`-wrapped helpers built for it (`DrawerMenuItemWithData`, lines 121-139; `ListMenuContentWithData`, lines 141-158) are fetched and constructed but have no effect on what renders. This is dead code specifically for nav purposes — I want to flag it precisely rather than assert it's dead in some absolute sense, since `_app/index.tsx` doesn't visibly use `categories` anywhere else either.

**`overrides/app/components/header/index.tsx`** — container for chrome/commerce state, presentational for layout
- Receives `children` (the `<DrawerMenu>`/`<ListMenu>` pair above) from `_app/index.tsx` as React children (lines 418-447), not as an explicit prop — it never imports `ListMenu`/`DrawerMenu`/`useHeaderNav` itself.
- Fetches its own non-nav commerce data directly (`useCurrentBasket`, `useCustomerType`, `useWishList`, lines 144-152) and owns mega-menu/drawer *UI* state via `useHeaderMenuExpandedState` (line 199) and the `MegaMenuOpenContext`/`DrawerMenuStateContext` providers (lines 232, 240) — no nav *data* fetching here.
- Passes the derived `menuExpanded`/`onClose` down to `LeftBar`/`RightBar` as props (lines 239, 242-259).

**`overrides/app/components/header/leftBar/index.tsx`** — pure presentational. Props: `children`, `onMenuClick`, `menuExpanded`, `onBack` (lines 10-24). Renders `children` (the nav) verbatim inside `<chakra.nav>` (line 99) — receives no nav data itself.

**`overrides/app/components/header/rightBar/index.tsx`** — pure presentational. Props listed lines 106-143 (`hasBasket`, `totalItems`, `isRegistered`, `filteredNavLinks`, `menuExpanded`, `onClose`, etc.), all sourced one level up from `header/index.tsx`. No nav-tree data.

**`overrides/app/components/list-menu/list-menu.tsx`** — this is the mega-menu container/view split, both in one file:
- `ListMenu` (container, lines 164-172): `const { items, isLoading } = useHeaderNav();` — **self-fetches**, ignoring `root`/`itemsKey`/`itemsCountKey`/`contentComponent` props it still declares for "call-site compatibility with base `_app.jsx`'s SFCC category-tree contract" (its own comment, lines 149-151).
- `ListMenuView` (presentational, lines 32-144): receives `items: ReadonlyArray<HeaderNavItemEntry> | undefined`, `isLoading`, `maxColumns` as props (lines 19-24) — fetches nothing.
- `HEADER_NAV_ITEMS_KEY = 'columns'` (line 17) is the field name `ListMenuPopover`/`MegaMenuContent` index into.

**`overrides/app/components/list-menu/list-menu-popover.tsx`** (override of base) — presentational, props at lines 59-105 (`item`, `name`, `itemsKey`, `isOpen`, `isActiveItem`, `motionPhase`, etc., all passed down from `ListMenuView`). Renders `ListMenuTrigger` + `ContentComponent` (`MegaMenuContent`, injected via prop).

**`overrides/app/components/list-menu/list-menu-trigger.tsx`** — presentational, props lines 8-38 (`item`, `name`, `isActive`, `onOpen/onClose/onEnterPanel`). Renders `ZimmNavItem`.

**`overrides/app/components/list-menu/megaMenuContent/index.tsx`** — presentational. Props `MegaMenuContentProps` (lines 56-85): `item: HeaderNavItemEntry`, `itemsKey`, `onClose`, `isFullyOpen`. Line 127: `const { columns, promoImage } = toMegaMenuItem(item, itemsKey);` — delegates all Contentful-shape knowledge to the adapter (its own doc comment, line 119: "All Contentful-shape knowledge is isolated in `toMegaMenuItem`").

**`overrides/app/components/list-menu/megaMenuContent/toMegaMenuItem.ts`** — the adapter, not a component. Pure function `toMegaMenuItem(item: HeaderNavItemEntry, itemsKey: string): MegaMenuItem` (line 36), maps raw Contentful `headerNavItem`/`navGroup`/`link` shapes into the presentational `MegaMenuItem`/`MegaMenuSection`/`MegaMenuLink` shapes defined in `types.ts`.

**`overrides/app/components/drawer-menu/index.tsx`** — same container/view split as list-menu:
- `DrawerMenu` (container, lines 263-291): `const { items, isLoading } = useHeaderNav();` (line 264) — **also self-fetches from Contentful**, ignoring `root`/`itemsKey`/`itemsCountKey`/`itemComponent` for the identical stated reason (lines 245-247: "an SFCC category-tree contract this component no longer reads from"). Also consumes `useDrawerMenuState()` (line 265) for L1/L2 UI drill state.
- `DrawerMenuView` (presentational, lines 134-240): props `items`, `isLoading`, `activeItem`, `isDrilledIn`, `onDrillInto`, `isOpen`, `onClose` (lines 40-52).

**`overrides/app/hooks/useHeaderNav.ts`** — the real nav-data hook (not `use-navigation.ts`). Full trace in §3/§4 below.

**`overrides/app/hooks/useDrawerMenuState.ts`**, **`useHeaderMenuExpandedState.ts`**, **`useMegaMenuMotion.ts`**, **`useMegaMenuOpenReporter.ts`**, **`useHeaderNavKeyboard.ts`** — all pure UI-state/choreography hooks (open/closed depth, motion phase machine, roving-focus, cross-tree open-state reporting via React Context). None of them fetch data or touch Contentful/SFCC; they take/return only UI state and `HeaderNavItemEntry` values already fetched elsewhere.

**`overrides/app/components/ui-kits/atoms/zimmNavItem/index.tsx`** — leaf presentational atom, props `label`, `href?`, `active?`, `visuallyActive?`, `variant?`, `growUnderline?`, `onClick/onMouseOver/onKeyDown` (lines 18-60). Renders `<button>` when `href` is omitted (line 22-25 comment). No data fetching.

## 2. The "nav item" / category node shape

There is no SFCC-category-shaped nav-item type in use. The real shape is Contentful-typed, in `overrides/app/types/contentful.ts`:

```ts
// lines 220-242
export type HeaderNavItemEntry = {
  sys: { id: string; contentType: { sys: { id: 'headerNavItem' } } };
  fields: {
    label: string;
    href?: string;                              // set only for a direct-link item
    readonly columns?: ReadonlyArray<NavGroupEntry>;  // 0/omitted = direct link; 1+ = mega-menu
    twoColumnLayout?: boolean;
    promoImage?: ImageEntry;                     // <-- the banner/promo field, see §4
    readonly regions?: ReadonlyArray<RegionEntry>;
  };
};

// lines 244-259
export type HeaderNavigationEntry = {
  sys: { id: string; contentType: { sys: { id: 'headerNavigation' } } };
  fields: {
    internalTitle: string;
    readonly items: ReadonlyArray<HeaderNavItemEntry>;
    readonly regions?: ReadonlyArray<RegionEntry>;
  };
};
```

`NavGroupEntry` (lines 134-153, shared with the footer) is `{ heading, links: LinkEntry[], showContactChannels? }`; `LinkEntry` (lines 112-126) is `{ label, href, regions? }`. The presentational layer re-shapes this via `toMegaMenuItem.ts` into `MegaMenuItem { columns: MegaMenuSection[][]; promoImage?: {src, alt} }` (`megaMenuContent/types.ts:7-26`) — deliberately isolating Contentful's shape from the rendering component.

## 3. Does the real nav hook call commerce-sdk-react for a category tree?

**No.** `overrides/app/hooks/useHeaderNav.ts` never imports `@salesforce/commerce-sdk-react`. Its only "commerce" import is the vendor `useMultiSite` (line 2), used solely for `site.id`/`locale.id`. The actual data fetch (lines 50-85) is:

```ts
const { site, locale: siteLocale } = useMultiSite() as MultiSiteResult;
...
const { client } = useContentfulClient();
const { data, isLoading, isError } = useQuery({
  queryKey: [HEADER_NAV_QUERY_KEY, site.id, locale],
  queryFn: async () => {
    const entries = await (client as ContentfulClientApi<undefined>)!.getEntries({
      content_type: CONTENT_TYPE_IDS.headerNavigation,
      include: HEADER_NAV_INCLUDE_DEPTH,   // = 4
      locale,
    });
    return entries.items as unknown as HeaderNavigationEntry[];
  },
  enabled: !!client,
});
```
(`CONTENT_TYPE_IDS.headerNavigation = 'headerNavigation'`, `overrides/app/config/contentfulMapping.ts:60`.) The only real SFCC `useCategory` call in the whole nav chain is the separate, effectively-unused one in `_app/index.tsx` documented in §1.

## 4. Contentful integration — the key question, answered precisely

Yes, and it's not a "merge" at all — **Contentful is the entire mega-menu/drawer data source**, end to end:

- Client: `overrides/app/hooks/useContentfulClient.ts:2` — `import { createClient } from 'contentful';` (real Contentful Delivery/Preview SDK), built at lines 56-59 from `getContentfulConfig()`.
- Fetch: `useHeaderNav.ts:64-68` (quoted above), content type `'headerNavigation'`.
- Region resolution: `useHeaderNav.ts:77-82` calls `pickMostSpecificByRegion` then `filterByRegion` (from `overrides/app/utils/resolveByRegion.ts:37,53`) to pick the right storefront-scoped entry.
- **The "banner/promo/featured" field is `promoImage`**, a native field on the `headerNavItem` content type itself — not a separate content type merged in:
  - Schema: `scripts/contentful/content-types/headerNavItem.js:56-64` — `{ id: 'promoImage', name: 'Promo Image', type: 'Link', linkType: 'Entry', validations: [{ linkContentType: ['image'] }] }`.
  - Type: `overrides/app/types/contentful.ts:235` — `promoImage?: ImageEntry;`.
  - Consumption (desktop/tablet): `megaMenuContent/toMegaMenuItem.ts:51` — `const promoImage = resolveImageEntry(item.fields.promoImage);`, rendered in `megaMenuContent/index.tsx:150-154`.
  - Consumption (mobile L2): `drawer-menu/index.tsx:163` — `const promoImage = isDrilledIn ? resolveImageEntry(activeItem?.fields.promoImage) : undefined;`, rendered lines 230-234.
  - `resolveImageEntry` (`overrides/app/utils/resolveImageEntry.ts:23-30`) resolves the Contentful `image` entry down to `{src, alt}`.

I also grepped the whole `overrides/app/` tree and `scripts/contentful/` for `banner|promo|featured` (case-insensitive) to check for any second, separate merge mechanism — every hit outside the nav chain is unrelated (ARIA `role="banner"`, `OfflineBanner`, homepage hero banner, PDP badges, etc.). There is exactly one other `getEntries({content_type: ...})` call site in the app (`footer/index.tsx:219`, `'footerConfig'`) — confirming `headerNavigation`/`headerNavItem` is the only Contentful nav integration, and it's real and wired, not a stub.

## 5. Gap / placeholder / stale comments found

Two genuine, currently-true gap comments, and one that is **stale** (claims a gap that's actually closed) — worth flagging since it could mislead someone into "fixing" something already done:

- **Real, current gap** — `overrides/app/hooks/useMegaMenuMotion.ts:109`: *"Desktop/tablet only — the mobile drawer (`drawer-menu/`) has no motion spec yet."* Confirmed: `drawer-menu/index.tsx:86-87` independently says *"No Figma motion spec exists for the L1<->L2 transition, so this swap is instant — a deliberate placeholder pending a real transition."*
- **Real, current gap** — `header/index.tsx:281-282`: mobile search bar is commented out, *"pending searchPopover implementation."* Related dead code at lines 100-112 (a whole unused `SearchBar` component, commented out).
- **Stale gap comment (verified via `git blame`)** — `overrides/app/components/header/headerTypes.ts:17-21` ("Scope note for SFCC-96/97... this branch (infra only) does not manage or derive this value from any real mega-menu/drawer open state... the header shell (`header/index.tsx`) does not pass one at all") and the matching doc comments in `leftBar/index.tsx:16-19,21-22` and `rightBar/index.tsx:133-138,140-141` ("Not wired to any real mega-menu/drawer state on this branch"). All four comment blocks trace to commit `ee9f1f23` (2026-08-27, "feat(header): add shared menuExpanded contract to RightBar/LeftBar"). But `header/index.tsx` **does** now derive and pass a real `menuExpanded` value — lines 164-211, especially 209-211:
  ```ts
  const menuExpanded: MenuExpandedState =
    mobileMenuExpanded !== 'closed' ? mobileMenuExpanded : isMegaMenuOpen ? 'fullSwap' : 'closed';
  ```
  passed at `header/index.tsx:239` (`<LeftBar menuExpanded={menuExpanded}>`) and `:257` (`<RightBar menuExpanded={menuExpanded}>`). `git blame` shows that wiring landed in commits `d9a064bb7`/`2b42527ab` (SFCC-96, mega-menu) and `a2a687ae5`/`82f12cb6` (SFCC-97, drawer) — the very next commits in the same branch, dated 2026-08-27/28. So the "not wired" comments are ~3 weeks stale as of today (2026-09-17); the feature is built, the comments just weren't updated after the follow-up landed.
- Also note (not a gap, but scoped-out by design): `list-menu.tsx:64-73` and `megaMenuContent/index.tsx:64-67` explicitly document `isOpen`/real popover state as "currently unused here... kept in the contract" — that's deliberate API surface, not an incompleteness marker.

## 6. Theme recipe files

`overrides/app/theme/components/listMenu.ts` and `header.ts` **do not exist** — the recipes live next to their components instead and are aggregated into `theme/components/index.ts:61-62,66-68` (`Header`, `ListMenu`, `ZimmDrawerMenu`, `ZimmHeaderLeftBar`, `ZimmHeaderRightBar`, `ZimmMegaMenuContent`). One sentence each on the two you asked about, plus the closely related ones:
- `header/header.css.ts` (`Header` recipe, base component's multi-part recipe): defines `baseStyle` only for its 17 parts (`container`, `topBar`, `logoBar`, `logo`, `icons`, `signout*`, etc., lines 6-28) — no `variants` map, i.e. no alternate visual states, just a single fixed style per part.
- `list-menu/list-menu.css.ts` (`ListMenu` recipe): also `baseStyle`-only (no `variants`), overriding `container` padding and a (currently unused, kept for base-theme compatibility per its own comment) `listMenuTriggerLink` style.
- `header/leftBar/leftBar.css.ts` / `header/rightBar/rightBar.css.ts` (`ZimmHeaderLeftBar`/`ZimmHeaderRightBar`): drive the responsive/`menuExpanded`-swap look (hamburger vs. bar vs. close) via shared breakpoints from `theme/components/headerShared.ts` (`BP.tablet`/`BP.desktop`).
- `list-menu/megaMenuContent/megaMenuContent.css.ts` (`ZimmMegaMenuContent`): the one recipe here that *does* take a variant — `useMultiStyleConfig(MEGA_MENU_CONTENT_RECIPE, { variant: isTwoColumn ? 'twoColumn' : undefined })` (`megaMenuContent/index.tsx:130`) for the one/two-column layout split.
- `theme/components/navConstants.ts`: not a recipe, just one shared constant, `NAV_LETTER_SPACING = '0'`, consumed by both `header.css.ts` and `list-menu.css.ts`.
